"tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#bonus-items-hidden-rewards","content":"Bonus items are given server-side when the reward is claimed. Players will see them appear in their inventory but won't see them during the roll animation."},"1625":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-21","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#custom-reward-types-with-hooks","content":"Use custom reward types to handle non-item rewards like vehicles or bank deposits. Register hooks in your own resource to handle these reward types."},"1626":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-22","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#lootbox-config-with-custom-rewards","content":"If a custom `rewardType` is set but no hook is registered, the system will log a warning and fall back to treating it as a regular item. This prevents rewards from being lost but may not give the intended reward."},"1627":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-23","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#removing-a-hook","content":"You can remove a previously registered hook if needed:"},"1628":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"page","content":"Framework Setup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Free Resources","Lootbox"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup"},"1629":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-0","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works","content":"How It Works"},"1630":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-1","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#ox_core--ox_inventory-setup","content":"ox_core + ox_inventory Setup"},"1631":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-2","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"Item Definition Format"},"1632":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-3","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"How It Works (ox_core)"},"1633":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-4","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Complete Example"},"1634":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-5","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order","content":"Resource Order"},"1635":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-6","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#qbcore--qbox-setup","content":"QBCore / Qbox Setup"},"1636":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-7","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"Item Definition Format"},"1637":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-8","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"How It Works (QBCore / Qbox)"},"1638":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-9","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Complete Example"},"1639":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-10","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"Resource Order"},"1640":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-11","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#reference-file","content":"Reference File"},"1641":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-12","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#adding-custom-lootboxes","content":"Adding Custom Lootboxes"},"1642":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-13","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1643":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-14","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"Item does nothing when used"},"1644":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-15","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#no-supported-framework-detected-warning","content":"\"No supported framework detected\" warning"},"1645":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-16","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#lootbox-opens-but-no-item-is-given","content":"Lootbox opens but no item is given"},"1646":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-17","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","content":"Each framework handles usable items differently. This page explains how to configure your item definitions so that lootbox cases work correctly with your framework and inventory system."},"1647":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-18","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","content":"These steps are **in addition** to defining your lootboxes in `config.lua`. You must also ensure the item definitions exist in your inventory/framework so players can hold and use the items."},"1648":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-19","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works","content":"When `config.registerUsableItems = true` (the default), sleepless\\_lootbox automatically registers each lootbox as a usable item through the framework bridge. However, the item must still be **defined** in your inventory or framework's item list — the resource can only register the *use callback*, not create the item definition itself."},"1649":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-20","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#ox_core--ox_inventory-setup","content":"When using **ox\\_core**, usable items are handled through **ox\\_inventory** item definitions rather than the framework itself. For each lootbox case item, you need to add a `server.export` entry in your ox\\_inventory item definitions that points back to this resource."},"1650":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-21","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `ox_inventory/data/items.lua`:"},"1651":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-22","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"The `server.export` value **must** follow the format `sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>`, where `<item_name>` matches the lootbox key defined in your `config.lua` or registered via exports. Without this, using the item will do nothing."},"1652":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-23","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"ox\\_inventory sees that the item has a `server.export` defined."},"1653":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-24","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"When a player uses the item, ox\\_inventory calls the matching export on `sleepless_lootbox`."},"1654":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-25","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The ox framework bridge registers these exports automatically when `config.registerUsableItems = true`."},"1655":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-26","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1656":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-27","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Here are all three default lootbox cases configured for ox\\_inventory:"},"1657":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-28","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Don't forget to also add item definitions for any **loot contents** (weapons, items, etc.) that your lootboxes can reward. Those items don't need `server.export` — only the case items do."},"1658":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-29","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order","content":"Make sure your `server.cfg` starts resources in the correct order:"},"1659":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-30","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#qbcore--qbox-setup","content":"When using **QBCore** or **Qbox**, lootbox case items must be defined in your shared items table with `useable = true`. This allows the framework to register usable item callbacks."},"1660":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-31","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `qb-core/shared/items.lua`:"},"1661":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-32","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"The `useable = true` flag is **required**. Without it, `QBCore.Functions.CreateUseableItem` (or `exports.qbx_core:CreateUseableItem` for Qbox) will not be able to register the callback, and using the item will do nothing."},"1662":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-33","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"The framework sees that the item has `useable = true` in the shared items table."},"1663":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"When `config.registerUsableItems = true`, the bridge calls `CreateUseableItem` for each lootbox."},"1664":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"When a player uses the item, the framework triggers the registered callback."},"1665":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1666":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-37","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Here are all three default lootbox cases configured for QBCore/Qbox:"},"1667":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-38","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Don't forget to also add item definitions for any **loot contents** (weapons, items, etc.) that your lootboxes can reward. Those items don't need `useable = true` — only the case items do."},"1668":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-39","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"Make sure your `server.cfg` starts resources in the correct order:"},"1669":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-40","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"For Qbox, replace `qb-core` with `qbx_core`:"},"1670":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-41","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#reference-file","content":"The resource includes a `_items.lua` reference file in its root directory containing example item definitions for both ox\\_inventory and QBCore/Qbox. This file is **not loaded at runtime** — it's purely for reference. Copy the relevant entries into your framework's item configuration."},"1671":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-42","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#adding-custom-lootboxes","content":"When you register a new lootbox (either in `config.lua` or via the `registerLootbox` export), you need to add a matching item definition to your framework:"},"1672":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-43","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**ox\\_inventory:** Verify the item definition includes `server.export = \"sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>\"` and that the item name matches your lootbox key exactly."},"1673":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**QBCore/Qbox:** Verify the item definition has `useable = true` in the shared items table."},"1674":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/lootb